  "notes": "Archnet and Arel describe the four iwans, six courtyard minarets with two more at the west entrance, tiled slender brick shafts, low dome, arcaded dormitory ranges, northeastern clock, and cross-shaped summer prayer hall. The Rietberg photograph establishes open balustraded minaret lanterns and profiles of vaults and pointed openings."
